{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Plan-review remediation round 3, against review rv10 (BLOCK; 1 blocking T8 + 5 advisory).\n\n- BLOCKING T8 (origin_decision undefined): correct — the reader unions blocking+advisory into one list, so a consumer could not tell a prior BLOCK from a prior ADVISORY. Fixed in code and plan: latest_code_review_result now stamps each surfaced item with the bucket it came from (blocking->block, advisory->advisory); standing_items copies that into standing.origin_decision, falling back to the item's own `decision` then to `advisory`, so the clamp can never invent a blocking posture.\n- E4 advisory (critical): my '_assemble_code_review_run is the only site holding session_id/change_id' claim was refuted by the snapshot — CodeReviewRequest carries both and is threaded to _run_code_review_gate/finalize too. Reworded: items resolve PRE-workflow in _assemble because that is where the workflow inputs are built, and the two sites now share ONE key rule via a new sidecar.memory_key that also replaces the key composition finalize.py open-coded.\n- E1/E6 advisory (critical): the dispatcher wiring had no AC. Added test_carried_findings_reach_only_the_post_pass1_merge_input in test_code_review_gate_session.py (asserts standing_findings is populated from the reader AND that the carried text appears in no finder-facing input) and an AC citing it.\n- T8 advisory (coverage): correct — the assembly-site coverage sink is not the signed coverage the coach step builds. The plan no longer claims per-state counts land in the signed coverage.\n- E6 advisory (unanchored grep): 'standing' also matches 'understanding'. The AC now greps -Eci 'standing finding|carried from an earlier patchset'.\n\nImplementation status: code, tests and gates are green in the worktree — make lint, make typecheck, complexity ratchet new=0 increased=0, all touched src/rebar files under the 800-line cap (workflow_ops.py 784, new carry_forward.py 215). Every new test was mutation-checked: 13 perturbations (flip the region->state mapping, drop the already-carried check, drop the grounded-only filter, drop the cap, skip the merge injection, inject a re-emitted item, no-op the clamp, blank the verify note, drop the Gerrit suffix, drop the adapter passthrough, drop the reader's revision key, ignore the origin_decision stamp, stamp both buckets the same) each turned a specific test RED."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787379294342622001,"uuid":"3ea34d53-c228-4186-b75c-b2d4a768308f"}